B.E2=s(["\u0a10\u0a24","\u0a38\u0a4b\u0a2e","\u0a2e\u0a70\u0a17\u0a32","\u0a2c\u0a41\u0a71\u0a27","\u0a35\u0a40\u0a30","\u0a38\u0a3c\u0a41\u0a71\u0a15\u0a30","\u0a38\u0a3c\u0a28\u0a3f\u0a71\u0a1a\u0a30"],t.s)
B.be7=new A.lO("Invite to the Oneness First","When the Prophet \ufdfa sent Mus\u2019ab to Madinah, he did not send rulings \u2014 he sent the shahada. The first question in dawah is never 'what about hijab' or 'what about politics' \u2014 it is 'who is Allah, and what does He ask of you?' Start where the revelation started.","In your next conversation about Islam, begin with Allah\u2019s mercy and oneness \u2014 not the rules. Let the heart open before the law arrives.")
B.be8=new A.lO("Wisdom Is Knowing the Person","Call to the way of your Lord with wisdom and good instruction, and argue with them in the best way (16:125). The same truth lands differently on a grieving friend, a skeptical coworker, and a curious child. The message is one; the door is tailored.",u.b4)
B.bed=new A.lO("The Taif Standard","When the people of Taif stoned him until his shoes filled with blood, the angel of the mountains came and offered to crush the city. The Prophet \ufdfa said: no \u2014 perhaps Allah will bring forth from them those who will worship Him alone (Bukhari 3231). The caller\u2019s job is to deliver, not to destroy.","When someone mocks your faith this week, respond with the Taif standard \u2014 no counter-mockery, no argument. Deliver the mercy, release the result.")
B.beb=new A.lO("Your Life Is the Loudest Sermon","The Prophet \ufdfa was called al-Amin \u2014 the trustworthy \u2014 before he was called a prophet. His character opened the door his words then walked through. The coworker who trusts your honesty will listen to your Islam; the one who has been burned by you will not.","Audit one relationship this week: does your character open the door or close it? Repair the one that closes it.")
B.aAV=s([B.be7,B.be8,B.bed,B.beb],t.Vs)
B.bej=new A.IY("The Method","The Prophet \ufdfa spent thirteen years in Makkah teaching one family, then one tribe, then a city. The method was patience, not pressure.",B.aAV)
B.be9=new A.lO('"Why Do Bad Things Happen?"',"Do not say about anything 'I will do that tomorrow' without adding 'if Allah wills' (18:23-24). And: perhaps you dislike a thing and it is good for you (2:216). The answer is not a theodicy lecture \u2014 it is the trust that the Author sees the whole book while we read one page.",u.cs)
B.bef=new A.lO('"Islam Is Too Strict."',"Allah intends for you ease and does not intend for you hardship (2:185). And: fear Allah as much as you are able (64:16). The deen has a floor and a ceiling; the caller shows the floor first \u2014 five prayers, honest work, kindness \u2014 and lets the person climb.","In your next conversation, describe Islam by its mercy (the door of repentance, the ease in hardship) before its boundaries.")
B.bec=new A.lO('"The Quran Was Written by a Man."',"Bring them a chapter like it \u2014 or ten chapters, or the whole book (2:23). The challenge stands 1400 years later. And ask: which man, alone in a cave, produces a book that billions memorize letter-by-letter while its author\u2019s enemies could not produce ten lines?",u.d2)
B.beg=new A.lO('"I Have Done Too Much Wrong."',"Say: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves \u2014 do not despair of the mercy of Allah; indeed, Allah forgives all sins (39:53). This is the verse for the one who thinks they are too far gone. The caller\u2019s task is to keep the door visibly open.","When someone confesses a sin to you, respond with 39:53 before any advice. The verse first, always.")
B.ao5=s([B.be9,B.bef,B.bec,B.beg],t.Vs)
B.beh=new A.IY("The Answers","The Qur\u2019an itself teaches how to answer: with the same verse that raised the question, and with the gentleness that carries it.",B.ao5)
B.bee=new A.lO("Gentleness Does Not Water Down the Truth","The Prophet \ufdfa said: gentleness is not found in anything except that it adds beauty to it, and it is not removed from anything except that it disgraces it (Muslim 2594). Musa was sent to Pharaoh \u2014 the worst tyrant in history \u2014 and Allah still commanded him: speak to him mildly (20:44).",u.aR)
B.bea=new A.lO("Knowledge Before Speech","Say: my Lord has only forbidden what is apparent of immorality and what is concealed (7:33). The caller must know before speaking \u2014 a half-answer delivered with confidence closes more doors than silence. When you do not know, say: I will find out. That sentence is dawah.","This week, when asked something you do not know, practice the sentence: 'That is a beautiful question \u2014 let me find out and come back to you.'")
B.be6=new A.lO("Release the Result","You are not over them a controller (88:22). Your job is to deliver the message clearly, kindly, and honestly; the heart that opens is Allah\u2019s to open. This releases the caller from the anxiety of rejection \u2014 you were never the one being rejected.",u.L)
B.aH3=s([B.bee,B.bea,B.be6],t.Vs)
B.bei=new A.IY("The Caller\u2019s Character","The message is carried by the messenger. These are the traits that make the carrier trustworthy.",B.aH3)
B.auV=s([B.bej,B.beh,B.bei],A.aa("y<IY>"))
