B.bgt=new A.d9(B.axL,"\u1e62\u0101d (\u0635) \u2014 It is a heavy letter: the back of the tongue rises towards the roof of the mouth, so the sound is full. Open the Letters school in the Academy and start the lesson for \u1e62\u0101d: you will see the letter, practise it and answer a gentle question. Say its name three times, slowly. Which letter did you learn just before this one?")
B.ar2=s(["dad heavy","heavy dad","\u1e0dad","duad","letter \u1e0dad","the \u1e0dad"],t.s)
B.bgL=new A.d9(B.ar2,"\u1e0c\u0101d (\u0636) \u2014 It is a heavy letter, made with the side of the tongue against the upper molars. Open the Letters school in the Academy and start the lesson for \u1e0c\u0101d: you will see the letter, practise it and answer a gentle question. Say its name three times, slowly. Which letter did you learn just before this one?")
B.aw1=s(["ta heavy","heavy ta","\u1e6da","toa","letter \u1e6da","the \u1e6da"],t.s)
